   "expected": "Top level has exactly the keys {date, host, checks}; date matches ^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$ and equals the subprocess's local date (do not hardcode; a UTC-vs-local midnight boundary is the only flake risk); host equals socket.gethostname() as seen by the child (do not assert a literal). 'checks' is a non-empty list; every element has exactly the 5 keys {group, item, status, detail, proof}; every status is in {verified, reported, unknown, MISSING}; every group is in GROUPS; the list is ordered so the first occurrence index of each group is non-decreasing (sorted by GROUPS index); 7 unique Tools items; 4 MCP rows; exactly 2 Open unknowns rows all unknown; 'checks' length equals the number of markdown table rows in the plain run (the two modes must not diverge).",
   "can_fail_because": "Any print before json.dumps in main (a debug line, or a warning routed to stdout) \u2192 json.loads red. Removing 'checks.sort(key=lambda c: GROUPS.index(c.group))' \u2192 group order red. Adding a field to Check but not to asdict output, or renaming 'proof' \u2192 the per-row key-set assertion red."
  },
  {
   "id": "RT-09",
   "name": "Markdown rendering: single heading per group, pipe escaping, 100-char truncation",
