   "action": "Run --json once WITHOUT --net and once WITH --net; compare logs and the login row.",
   "expected": "Without --net: Tools row agy verified 'agy-fake 1.2.14'; 'agy login (model list)' row status unknown, detail 'offline run: not provable without `agy models`; rerun with --net', proof '`agy models` (network)'; rc 0; and the log holds exactly one line '--version' \u2014 no network command is issued unless asked. With --net: log holds '--version' and 'models' (two lines only, nothing else \u2014 no qwen/agy prompt); login row status verified with detail '3 models: gemini-9-pro, gemini-9-flash, gpt-oss-120b-medium \u2026' \u2014 the 'Fetching\u2026' banner is filtered by the lower().startswith('fetching') guard and blank/whitespace lines by 'if l.split()', the ids[:4] slice is not reached so no id is dropped, and the trailing '\u2026' is printed unconditionally even for 3 ids (assert it literally). rc 0 both runs.",
   "can_fail_because": "Delete the 'if not net' early return (run agy models always) \u2192 the offline run's log gains a 'models' line and its row flips to verified \u2192 both halves red, which is the point: this is the second no-network-by-default guard. Or drop the startswith('fetching') filter \u2192 detail becomes '4 models: Fetching\u2026, \u2026' red; or change 'ids[:4]' \u2192 'ids[:2]' \u2192 the shown list truncates red."
  },
  {
   "id": "RT-13",
   "name": "--blueprint / --workflows flags and argparse usage errors (exit 2)",
   "setup": "tmp cwd; bp/ holding README.md, a.md, b.md, notes.txt; wf/ holding a.js, b.js, tool.py, .hidden.js; nope/ does not exist. Fake bin PATH (all binaries MISSING) so no real tool runs in any sub-run.",
   "action": "Six runs: (a) --blueprint bp ; (b) --blueprint nope --json ; (c) --workflows wf ; (d) --nope ; (e) --blueprint (no DIR) ; (f) --require a b.",
   "expected": "(a) rc 0, row 'blueprint (<abs path of bp>)' status verified, detail '3 sections, map present: README.md, a.md, b.md' (notes.txt excluded by the .md filter, has_map from README.md). (b) status MISSING detail 'directory not found' and rc **1** \u2014 an explicitly named blueprint is a hard fail, unlike an absent default directory, and this is the ONLY non---require path that exits 1. (c) exactly one 'workflow scripts' row, detail '2: a.js, b.js' (list_names keeps dirs and .js/.mjs/.md, skips dotfiles, drops tool.py), proof = the wf path; the default .claude/workflows row is replaced, not added. (d)(e)(f) rc 2, argparse usage text on stderr, and stdout empty \u2014 no inventory, no partial JSON.",
   "can_fail_because": "Delete the blueprint loop in exit_code, or typo 'c.item.startswith(\"blueprint (\")' to '\"blueprint\"'-less form / 'checks' order so it never matches \u2192 (b) exits 0 red. Or 'if e.suffix == \".md\"' \u2192 '!= \".md\"' \u2192 (a) reports '1 sections, map MISSING' red. Or give --blueprint nargs='?' \u2192 (e) exits 0 instead of 2 red."
  },
  {
   "id": "RT-14",
   "name": "--self-test proves the gate can fail, and fails honestly when it cannot",
   "setup": "Run 1: sanitized env, fake bin PATH with the 7 fakes, none named 'readiness-selftest-fake-tool'; make the fakes log argv (reuse the RT-11 logger) so an inventory run can be detected. Run 2: a bin dir that additionally contains an executable named readiness-selftest-fake-tool printing 'fake 1.0' and exit 0.",
   "action": "Run '--self-test' in both, plus '--self-test --json' in run 1.",
   "expected": "Run 1: rc 0, stdout is exactly one line containing 'self-test PASS: `readiness-selftest-fake-tool` reported MISSING and --require on it exits 1 \u2014 the check can fail.'; no '#' heading, no '| Item | Status' header, and the fake binaries' log stays empty \u2014 self_test() returns before gather(), so the self-test is cheap and offline. Run 2: rc 1 with 'self-test FAIL: status=verified, exit code=0 (expected MISSING, 1)' \u2014 the self-test must not report PASS on a machine where the fake tool name exists. '--self-test --json': rc 0, the PASS line, and stdout must NOT parse as JSON (the flag wins over the output mode).",
   "can_fail_because": "In self_test(), check only 'c.status == MISSING' and ignore the exit code (or 'return 0' unconditionally as a stub) \u2192 run 2 exits 0 with no FAIL line red \u2014 that is the whole purpose: it proves the --require gate is live, not decorative. Symmetric mutation in exit_code: 'return 1' \u2192 'return 0' turns run 1's PASS into 'self-test FAIL: status=MISSING, exit code=0' with rc 1 red."
  }
 ]
